5264
06:41:32.100 --> 06:41:34.560
The RSA figures tell us that very clearly.

5265
06:41:35.160 --> 06:41:39.040
There has been enormous progress over the
longer term; we should acknowledge that.

5266
06:41:39.560 --> 06:41:43.580
Ireland has gone from hundreds of road
deaths a year to figures that, for a

5267
06:41:43.580 --> 06:41:45.120
period, were among the best in Europe.

5268
06:41:45.920 --> 06:41:49.960
That progress is not something we should
take for granted, but I fear that the eye

5269
06:41:49.960 --> 06:41:51.020
has been taken off the ball.

5270
06:41:51.620 --> 06:41:56.840
The RSA's long-term figures show a rise in
road deaths from 134 in 2018 to

5271
06:41:56.840 --> 06:41:58.600
185 in 2025.

5272
06:41:59.180 --> 06:42:04.000
The Garda figures report 190 deaths in
2025 as they include deaths in public

5273
06:42:04.000 --> 06:42:06.800
places such as car parks and private
roads.

5274
06:42:07.160 --> 06:42:11.460
The Bill does not address this but we also
need to clarify which are the more

5275
06:42:11.460 --> 06:42:14.730
accurate figures when it comes to deaths
as a result of cars.

5276
06:42:14.730 --> 06:42:19.680
I would argue that the Garda figures are
more complete in that regard but that is a

5277
06:42:19.680 --> 06:42:20.520
discussion for another day.

5278
06:42:21.840 --> 06:42:25.780
Tragically, regardless of whose figures we
use - those of the Garda or the RSA - the

5279
06:42:25.780 --> 06:42:29.120
trend of increasing fatalities shows no
signs of reversing this year.

5280
06:42:29.440 --> 06:42:34.320
At the end of July, 105 people had already
lost their lives on Irish roads, or 13

5281
06:42:34.320 --> 06:42:34.840
more than

5282
06:42:34.840 --> 06:42:36.180
the same point in 2025.

5283
06:42:37.640 --> 06:42:40.800
More than 40% of fatalities occurred on
Saturdays and Sundays.

5284
06:42:41.160 --> 06:42:44.430
The RSA reports that 57% of fatalities
occurred on roads

5285
06:42:47.700 --> 06:42:50.800
27% of those killed were aged between 16
and 25.

5286
06:42:51.560 --> 06:42:55.680
Every one of these road fatalities and
every life lost will have left devastation

5287
06:42:55.680 --> 06:42:59.000
in its wake for the thousands of people
grieving the loss of their loved one.

5288
06:42:59.000 --> 06:43:01.740
We have all seen the consequences in our
communities.

5289
06:43:02.420 --> 06:43:05.820
In February, a man in his 80s, Frank Daly,
was killed when a Bus Éireann

5290
06:43:05.820 --> 06:43:09.300
double-decker bus struck pedestrians not
far from here on North Earl Street.

5291
06:43:09.860 --> 06:43:11.110
Three other people were taken to hospital.

5292
06:43:11.780 --> 06:43:15.860
In June, a man in his 30s died following a
three-car collision on the M21 between

5293
06:43:15.860 --> 06:43:17.220
Abbeyfeale and Newcastle West.

5294
06:43:17.720 --> 06:43:20.500
His death brought the number of people
killed on Irish roads at that point in the

5295
06:43:20.500 --> 06:43:22.600
year to 75, six higher than

5296
06:43:22.600 --> 06:43:23.220
the previous year.

5297
06:43:23.800 --> 06:43:27.760
In July, three men were killed in separate
collisions in Donegal, Cork and Kildare in

5298
06:43:27.760 --> 06:43:28.740
the space of a single day.

5299
06:43:29.340 --> 06:43:33.400
In August, we witnessed an absolutely
devastating collision on the M9 in

5300
06:43:33.400 --> 06:43:37.630
Kildare, where five teenagers lost their
lives in a head-on collision after a car

5301
06:43:39.980 --> 06:43:43.460
Four other people, a family including a
child who were on their way to Dublin

5302
06:43:43.460 --> 06:43:45.280
Airport to go on holiday, were seriously
injured.

5303
06:43:45.280 --> 06:43:47.000
I am so glad to

5304
06:43:47.000 --> 06:43:47.800
an update from

5305
06:43:47.800 --> 06:43:51.560
three sisters yesterday to say they are
getting stronger each day, and I wish them

5306
06:43:51.560 --> 06:43:53.760
the very best as they continue their
recovery.

5307
06:43:54.600 --> 06:43:57.760
These sorts of devastating events stay
with communities.

5308
06:43:58.040 --> 06:44:01.900
They stay with the emergency workers who
respond to them - the gardaí and anyone

5309
06:44:01.900 --> 06:44:05.220
who happens to witness them - and above
all, they stay with the families who are

5310
06:44:05.220 --> 06:44:05.940
impacted by them.

5311
06:44:06.720 --> 06:44:09.560
The barometer against which we have to
measure every piece of road traffic

5312
06:44:09.620 --> 06:44:13.060
legislation, such as this one, is whether
it will make our roads safer.

5313
06:44:13.060 --> 06:44:18.800
On the data-sharing element of this, I am
confident this Bill will do that.

5314
06:44:18.800 --> 06:44:22.660
On the speed limits element, though, which
comes under Part 5 of the Bill, I cannot

5315
06:44:22.660 --> 06:44:24.010
say I am quite as convinced.

5316
06:44:24.600 --> 06:44:27.040
In fact, I find this part of the Bill a
little

5317
06:44:28.280 --> 06:44:31.680
Section 21 provides for local authorities
to be able to continue to set a special

5318
06:44:31.680 --> 06:44:35.820
speed limit of 60 km/h for local roads in
