default urban speed limit of 30 km/h.

5321
06:44:44.720 --> 06:44:45.920
I support this campaign.

5322
06:44:46.660 --> 06:44:51.240
At the very least, the sensible approach
would be to standardise urban road speed

5323
06:44:51.240 --> 06:44:51.520
limits.

5324
06:44:52.080 --> 06:44:53.650
At present, a road

5325
06:44:57.220 --> 06:44:59.180
different area, it would be 50 km/h.

5326
06:44:59.180 --> 06:45:02.860
It creates ambiguity, and when it comes to
road safety and the rules of the road,

5327
06:45:02.860 --> 06:45:05.120
ambiguity poses a genuine danger.

5328
06:45:05.260 --> 06:45:09.760
It also sends the wrong message about
allowing higher speeds in built-up areas.

5329
06:45:10.620 --> 06:45:12.120
Drivers could legitimately ask why

5330
06:45:12.280 --> 06:45:13.200
okay for one road to

5331
06:45:13.300 --> 06:45:13.680
60

5332
06:45:13.680 --> 06:45:14.360
but another

5333
06:45:14.360 --> 06:45:14.720
50

5334
06:45:14.720 --> 06:45:15.980
in very similar areas.

5335
06:45:16.580 --> 06:45:20.700
They may be tempted to put the foot down a
little bit more as a result, seeing a sort

5336
06:45:20.700 --> 06:45:21.940
of unfairness there.

5337
06:45:22.660 --> 06:45:27.300
My clear position is that we should be
reducing urban speed limits to 30 km/h.

5338
06:45:27.300 --> 06:45:30.220
It is increasingly becoming the
international norm.

5339
06:45:30.220 --> 06:45:34.020
It is also the policy direction that this
State has already legislated for.

5340
06:45:34.500 --> 06:45:37.040
The Road Traffic Act 2024 provided for

5341
06:45:37.040 --> 06:45:40.600
a

5342
06:45:40.600 --> 06:45:41.960
was hardly dry on that Act,

5343
06:45:41.960 --> 06:45:43.950
before the Government started to roll back
on it.

5344
06:45:43.950 --> 06:45:47.660
I have tabled a number of parliamentary
questions to try to ascertain why the

5345
06:45:47.660 --> 06:45:51.300
Government was effectively moving away
from the national default approach and

5346
06:45:51.300 --> 06:45:55.880
instead instructing local authorities to
introduce 30 km/h speed limits through

5347
06:45:55.880 --> 06:45:57.180
special speed limit zones.

5348
06:45:57.180 --> 06:45:59.720
I have never really received a
satisfactory response.

5349
06:45:59.720 --> 06:46:02.560
Generally, all I get is that

5350
06:46:02.580 --> 06:46:03.120
too difficult.

5351
06:46:03.120 --> 06:46:04.700
Once again,

5352
06:46:04.700 --> 06:46:05.460
not good enough.

5353
06:46:06.060 --> 06:46:10.100
The question should not be about whether
moving from 50 km/h to 30 km/h speed

5354
06:46:10.100 --> 06:46:11.740
limits in built-up areas is difficult or
not.

5355
06:46:12.240 --> 06:46:15.480
It should be about whether it would save
lives and prevent serious injuries.

5356
06:46:16.100 --> 06:46:20.700
The relationship between speed and the
severity of pedestrian collisions is well

5357
06:46:20.700 --> 06:46:20.940
established.

5358
06:46:21.500 --> 06:46:26.140
Around 5% of pedestrians would be killed
at an impact speed of 30 km/h, compared

5359
06:46:26.140 --> 06:46:31.900
with approximately 50% at 60 km/h and 90%
at 80 km/h.

5360
06:46:31.900 --> 06:46:34.120
There is an extraordinary difference
there.

5361
06:46:34.180 --> 06:46:37.100
At 30 km/h, we give someone a fighting
chance.

5362
06:46:37.640 --> 06:46:41.990
At higher speeds, the consequences of a
mistake become drastically, dramatically

5363
06:46:43.400 --> 06:46:46.540
Speed limits are not about how we get
drivers from A to B most efficiently.

5364
06:46:46.540 --> 06:46:51.260
They are about what happens when something
goes wrong, like a child running out onto

5365
06:46:51.260 --> 06:46:54.910
a road, a cyclist falling off their bike
in the middle of traffic or a driver

5366
06:46:57.800 --> 06:47:01.510
We cannot build a road system around the
assumption that everyone will behave

5367
06:47:03.080 --> 06:47:08.020
Our road system should be designed so that
those mistakes do not automatically become

5368
06:47:08.020 --> 06:47:10.540
fatal or risk life-changing injuries for
those

5369
06:47:11.660 --> 06:47:16.200
The case for reducing urban speed limits
to 30 km/h is clear, based on the evidence

5370
06:47:16.200 --> 06:47:18.000
from places where this has been done.

5371
06:47:18.800 --> 06:47:19.060
Wales, for

5372
06:47:23.420 --> 06:47:25.220
built-up areas in September 2023.

5373
06:47:25.940 --> 06:47:30.300
Early evidence showed average speeds
falling by around 4 miles per hour on a

5374
06:47:30.300 --> 06:47:30.960
sample of main roads.

5375
06:47:31.460 --> 06:47:36.180
In 2024, casualties on roads in Wales with
20 miles per hour and 30 miles per hour

5376
06:47:36.180 --> 06:47:39.080
limits combined were almost 20% lower than

5377
06:47:39.080 --> 06:47:40.100
the year before.

5378
06:47:40.100 --> 06:47:44.180
It is a relatively short period of data
but the direction of travel is

5379
06:47:44.180 --> 06:47:44.580
encouraging.

5380
06:47:44.580 --> 06:47:47.700
It is certainly a lot better than the
direction we have been heading in for some

5381
06:47:47.700 --> 06:47:48.300
time now here.

5382
06:47:48.880 --> 06:47:53.100
The Welsh Government has also estimated
that the introduction of 20 miles per hour

5383
06:47:53.100 --> 06:47:58.280
limits could prevent deaths and serious
injuries while delivering wider economic

5384
06:47:58.280 --> 06:47:59.460
and public health benefits.

5385
06:48:00.000 --> 06:48:01.370
We can also look to Spain.

5386
06:48:01.940 --> 06:48:06.760
They introduced a nationwide urban 30 km/h
limit on streets with a single lane in

5387
06:48:06.760 --> 06:48:08.380
each direction in 2021.

5388
06:48:09.920 --> 06:48:14.000
Urban road deaths fell by 20% in 2021
compared with 2019.

5389
06:48:14.740 --> 06:48:19.120
Their directorate general for traffic
specifically linked the reduction to a

5390
06:48:19.120 --> 06:48:21.340
package of urban road safety measures,
including

5391
06:48:21.340 --> 06:48:23.480
30 km/h limit.

5392
06:48:24.200 --> 06:48:29.860
Pedestrian deaths fell by 26%, cyclist
deaths by 34% and deaths among people over

5393
06:48:29.860 --> 06:48:31.840
64 by 31%.

5394
06:48:31.840 --> 06:48:37.360
Five years on, Spain continues to see a
positive trend, with urban fatalities in

5395
06:48:37.360 --> 06:48:43.300
2024 5% below 2019 levels, while cyclist
fatalities in cities were almost 19%

5396
06:48:43.600 --> 06:48:46.840
lower and pedestrian fatalities more than
16% lower.

5397
06:48:47.560 --> 06:48:51.440
The case for reducing urban speed limits
as a default is not theoretical.

5398
06:48:52.020 --> 06:48:55.500
This is what happens when governments
decide that speed in urban areas should be

5399
06:48:55.500 --> 06:48:59.700
designed around the safety of humans
rather than the convenience of the fastest

5400
06:48:59.700 --> 06:49:00.620
possible journey.

5401
06:49:01.380 --> 06:49:05.990
I pay particular tribute to the Love 30
campaign group, which has been to the fore

5402
06:49:11.180 --> 06:49:15.820
particularly in town centres, residential
areas and around schools and places of

5403
06:49:15.820 --> 06:49:16.460
public assembly.

5404
06:49:16.720 --> 06:49:20.700
I had the pleasure of hosting Love 30 here
in Leinster House for an audiovisual room

5405
06:49:20.700 --> 06:49:24.370
briefing on the campaign, alongside other
organisations including the Dublin

5406
06:49:28.880 --> 06:49:32.470
the Irish Road Victims Association and
community groups from around the country,

5407
06:49:37.320 --> 06:49:41.380
Whether it is pedestrians, cyclists,
children on their way to school, older

5408
06:49:41.380 --> 06:49:45.740
people going to do their shopping, people
with disabilities navigating pavements and

5409
06:49:45.740 --> 06:49:49.940
crossings, commuters waiting for a bus or
teenagers hanging out with friends, we

5410
06:49:49.940 --> 06:49:54.440
have to design our roads and institute a
road safety system for all of these

5411
06:49:54.440 --> 06:49:54.700
people.

5412
06:49:55.440 --> 06:49:57.910
We also have to keep an eye on
enforcement.

5413
06:49:58.540 --> 06:49:59.500
the other side of this debate.

5414
06:49:59.960 --> 06:50:00.760
A speed limit that

5415
06:50:00.920 --> 06:50:02.920
enforced is just a number on a sign.

5416
06:50:03.380 --> 06:50:06.660
There was a 23% increase in motorists
caught speeding last year.

5417
06:50:07.200 --> 06:50:07.210
I

5418
06:50:07.320 --> 06:50:11.960
