are breaking the law, we will not be able

6180
07:37:08.290 --> 07:37:08.930
to enforce the law.

6181
07:37:08.930 --> 07:37:09.130
If

6182
07:37:10.670 --> 07:37:11.570
take home today,

6183
07:37:11.570 --> 07:37:13.510
is enforcement.

6184
07:37:13.510 --> 07:37:18.970
However, to be honest, I believe there
will be fewer than 600 people policing our

6185
07:37:18.970 --> 07:37:22.910
roads in five years' time, unfortunately.

6186
07:37:27.550 --> 07:37:33.450
As an Opposition TD who tries to be
constructive, I broadly welcome the

6187
07:37:33.450 --> 07:37:37.050
National Vehicle and Driver File, Road
Traffic and Roads Bill 2026.

6188
07:37:38.710 --> 07:37:43.410
Many elements of it are welcome and will
bring driving regulations and monitoring

6189
07:37:43.410 --> 07:37:45.600
somewhat into the 21st century.

6190
07:37:45.990 --> 07:37:51.710
The decision to finally abolish the paper
motor tax discs is an important

6191
07:37:51.710 --> 07:37:52.090
measure.

6192
07:37:52.690 --> 07:37:56.750
For decades we forced motorists to have
this piece of paper on their windscreens

6193
07:37:56.750 --> 07:38:00.570
while the rest of society moved ahead with
digitalisation.

6194
07:38:00.570 --> 07:38:05.330
As such, moving to a digital system,
backed by an online verification portal,

6195
07:38:05.330 --> 07:38:11.006
makes a lot of sense, just as it did in
the UK perhaps 14 years ago.

6196
07:38:11.006 --> 07:38:13.150
I will mention the

6197
07:38:13.150 --> 07:38:14.790
issue of insurance discs in a while.

6198
07:38:19.930 --> 07:38:24.105
The introduction of open-ended non-use
declarations also makes sense, as it will

6199
07:38:24.105 --> 07:38:29.620
get rid of an unnecessary layer of
bureaucracy for thousands of vintage

6200
07:38:33.470 --> 07:38:38.030
people who fix cars and citizens who have
their car off the road for whatever

6201
07:38:38.030 --> 07:38:38.410
reason.

6202
07:38:38.410 --> 07:38:44.370
Removing some of the bureaucracy is very

6203
07:38:44.370 --> 07:38:44.790
welcome.

6204
07:38:45.870 --> 07:38:49.870
also welcome the legal framework to
finally resume the sharing of traffic

6205
07:38:49.870 --> 07:38:50.770
collision data between

6206
07:38:50.770 --> 07:38:53.330
Garda Síochána and local authorities.

6207
07:38:54.270 --> 07:39:00.110
This is crucial but has been unfortunately
delayed because councils cannot engineer

6208
07:39:00.110 --> 07:39:04.590
safer roads if they do not have full
information about where accidents are

6209
07:39:04.590 --> 07:39:06.290
occurring.

6210
07:39:06.290 --> 07:39:09.990
In this context, while the Bill is a
welcome step, this Government and its

6211
07:39:09.990 --> 07:39:13.290
predecessor have already failed the
broader test of dealing with the deadly

6212
07:39:13.290 --> 07:39:15.360
crisis unfolding on our roads.

6213
07:39:15.360 --> 07:39:19.470
As we all know, we are in the middle of a
devastating spike in road fatalities,

6214
07:39:19.470 --> 07:39:21.630
which are up significantly on

6215
07:39:21.630 --> 07:39:22.490
2025.

6216
07:39:22.570 --> 07:39:24.270
Depending on which figures

6217
07:39:24.570 --> 07:39:30.270
up 17% on last year and are rising at a
time when the European Union average is

6218
07:39:30.270 --> 07:39:30.710
falling.

6219
07:39:30.710 --> 07:39:33.750
That is shocking and concerning.

6220
07:39:34.650 --> 07:39:35.100
The crisis

6221
07:39:38.350 --> 07:39:40.590
the delay in delivering this Bill as an
example,

6222
07:39:41.870 --> 07:39:46.030
the previous Government allowed strict
GDPR limitations and interpretations to

6223
07:39:46.030 --> 07:39:51.590
legally block councils from getting
collision data since November 2023, even

6224
07:39:51.590 --> 07:39:56.430
though the Data Protection Commission
explicitly stated that GDPR should not

6225
07:39:56.430 --> 07:40:02.020
prevent proportionate publication of crash
location details, especially when the

6226
07:40:02.020 --> 07:40:07.960
technology exists to get rid of personal
identifiers by anonymising or

6227
07:40:07.960 --> 07:40:09.040
limiting the data.

6228
07:40:09.440 --> 07:40:15.320
The critics of this asked why the RSA
could not just itself strip

6229
07:40:15.320 --> 07:40:19.300
out names and addresses or pass on the
co-ordinates to council engineers.

6230
07:40:19.300 --> 07:40:20.890
I am wondering

6231
07:40:24.380 --> 07:40:24.940
It

6232
07:40:24.940 --> 07:40:27.420
meant that for three years local
authorities have been effectively

6233
07:40:27.420 --> 07:40:28.000
blindfolded.

6234
07:40:28.740 --> 07:40:32.980
I acknowledge there are patch jobs that
were put in, like the locations of

6235
07:40:32.980 --> 07:40:38.680
interest, so they got some statistics, but
one has to ask how many

6236
07:40:38.680 --> 07:40:44.670
accident black spots went unfixed while
this Bill was just dragging

6237
07:40:51.240 --> 07:40:56.880
this Bill brings in digital tracking

6238
07:40:57.200 --> 07:41:03.000
and makes things a lot easier, it is, as
other Deputies have said, very quiet on

6239
07:41:03.000 --> 07:41:04.320
the enforcement of the law.

6240
07:41:04.320 --> 07:41:07.600
It is great to have a database, but if we

6241
07:41:07.700 --> 07:41:12.850
have enough traffic corps members on the
roads to intercept dangerous drivers, it

6242
07:41:12.850 --> 07:41:14.050
will not work.

6243
07:41:14.050 --> 07:41:19.000
That is why, as I have said before, we
need a separate dedicated traffic police

6244
07:41:19.000 --> 07:41:22.480
whose members have specific powers in
relation to the roads and who do not even

6245
07:41:22.480 --> 07:41:23.360
have to be members of

6246
07:41:23.360 --> 07:41:23.940
Garda Síochána.

6247
07:41:24.300 --> 07:41:26.900
That is a model that works in other
countries.

6248
07:41:29.620 --> 07:41:34.450
The databases that we will improve on will
not breathalyse the drivers.

6249
07:41:35.640 --> 07:41:40.560
I take on board what Deputy Tóibín said
about being stopped and breathalysed at 10

6250
07:41:40.560 --> 07:41:40.920
in the morning.

6251
07:41:41.000 --> 07:41:44.820
I was breathalysed by a garda at 8 o'clock
in the morning.

6252
07:41:44.880 --> 07:41:46.180
I said, "You are on the ball."

6253
07:41:46.500 --> 07:41:50.220
He said that it was part of Drew's
measures and that they had to do that

6254
07:41:50.220 --> 07:41:51.740
before they clocked off.

6255
07:41:52.380 --> 07:41:58.140
To me, it makes more sense to try to catch
people when they are actually under the

6256
07:41:58.140 --> 07:41:58.150
influence.

6257
07:41:59.840 --> 07:42:05.080
We do not have new digital measures
stopping and seizing unroadworthy vehicles

6258
07:42:05.080 --> 07:42:05.620
when

6259
07:42:05.760 --> 07:42:06.620
actually on the road.

6260
07:42:06.620 --> 07:42:11.340
Yes, it can be traced back, but sometimes
you have to stop the people when

6261
07:42:11.420 --> 07:42:12.240
actually out there.

6262
07:42:12.700 --> 07:42:14.300
You nab them on the spot.

6263
07:42:16.100 --> 07:42:20.880
bugbear of mine is the person who drives
for a full kilometre in a bus lane.

6264
07:42:21.620 --> 07:42:24.300
The R136 in my constituency is a case in
point.

6265
07:42:25.200 --> 07:42:28.530
I have a lot of sympathy for people who,
if

6266
07:42:28.680 --> 07:42:32.800
turning towards a left lane, get into the
bus lane so as to avoid queuing.

6267
07:42:32.800 --> 07:42:36.960
They are not blocking any buses and not
blocking any traffic and are able to make

6268
07:42:36.960 --> 07:42:39.620
a turn, but how long is a piece of string?

6269
07:42:39.620 --> 07:42:45.400
I have seen people go along for the full
kilometre and then bump in front of

6270
07:42:45.400 --> 07:42:45.940
someone else.

6271
07:42:46.620 --> 07:42:46.940
That

6272
07:42:46.940 --> 07:42:50.640
irritates other drivers and is breaking
the law but it is increasing.

6273
07:42:50.640 --> 07:42:54.860
I have seen it anecdotally a lot more in
the past two or three years than I

6274
07:42:55.000 --> 07:42:56.560
in the previous ten.

6275
07:42:56.560 --> 07:43:01.380
I have had reports from constituents of
those idiots who break the pedestrian

6276
07:43:01.380 --> 07:43:05.440
lights in heavy traffic, not just when

6277
07:43:05.560 --> 07:43:10.500
going at speed but also when they are
going to work during school times, when

6278
07:43:10.500 --> 07:43:11.340
the traffic is busy.

6279
07:43:11.900 --> 07:43:15.580
They go through the lights and sometimes
push past the school traffic wardens as

6280
07:43:15.580 --> 07:43:15.590
well.

6281
07:43:16.740 --> 07:43:18.700
We need that physical element of policing.

6282
07:43:19.340 --> 07:43:22.680
We also have to look at the gaps that the
legislation fails to fill.

6283
07:43:23.280 --> 07:43:27.800
I again refer to Jax's law, which I was
happy to co-sign recently.

6284
07:43:28.380 --> 07:43:28.390
I

6285
07:43:28.540 --> 07:43:31.640
repeat everything Deputy Barry Ward, who
is proposing it along with Deputy Currie,

6286
07:43:31.700 --> 07:43:37.380
said earlier, but this legislation
highlights one of the important gaps in

6287
07:43:37.380 --> 07:43:40.060
our core road traffic framework, that

6288
07:43:40.060 --> 07:43:45.080
the law still fails to legally recognise
the loss of an unborn child caused by

6289
07:43:45.080 --> 07:43:45.760
dangerous driving.

6290
07:43:47.260 --> 07:43:51.800
If the Government is fully committed to
comprehensive reform, mechanisms to

6291
07:43:51.800 --> 07:43:56.550
address gaps like Jax's law could be
integrated into this legislation, as

6292
07:43:57.480 --> 07:44:03.400
The Department should do it rather than
waiting for Deputy Ward to put the

6293
07:44:03.400 --> 07:44:04.480
amendment in himself.

6294
07:44:05.560 --> 07:44:10.480
That would be better than having grieving
families campaigning on the margins,

6295
07:44:11.000 --> 07:44:11.480
hoping that

6296
07:44:11.540 --> 07:44:15.280
gets to Second Stage and other Stages
through other means.

6297
07:44:15.820 --> 07:44:18.680
If Jax's law could be added into the
wording, I would certainly support

6298
07:44:18.680 --> 07:44:19.800
amendments to that effect.

6299
07:44:20.640 --> 07:44:26.300
Earlier today, I mentioned the lack of
joined-up thinking in transport

6300
07:44:26.300 --> 07:44:30.620
and planning as regards buses, trains,
parking spaces and EV charging facilities

6301
07:44:30.620 --> 07:44:31.900
in new developments.

6302
07:44:33.480 --> 07:44:37.260
People are told they cannot have parking
spaces because they have this fantastic

6303
07:44:37.260 --> 07:44:38.420
public transport service,

6304
07:44:39.700 --> 07:44:43.250
so they have to drive but they have
nowhere to park.

6305
07:44:44.140 --> 07:44:46.260
People get frustrated because of this.

6306
07:44:46.960 --> 07:44:47.660
They get agitated.

6307
07:44:47.660 --> 07:44:50.220
They have been fighting with their
neighbour to try to get a parking space.

6308
07:44:50.660 --> 07:44:54.140
Now they are rushing out to get to a place
that you need to take three buses,

6309
07:44:54.140 --> 07:44:54.920
to get to.

6310
07:44:58.300 --> 07:45:02.740
We have to understand what is required in
new developments.

6311
07:45:03.780 --> 07:45:03.920
If

6312
07:45:04.040 --> 07:45:10.000
going forward, all speeds in new
developments should be 10 km/h - as

6313
07:45:10.000 --> 07:45:15.680
simple as that - not the 30 km/h and 10
km/h and then a crawl out of it allowing

6314
07:45:15.680 --> 07:45:19.360
people to move at normal speed, but
allowing people to actually park their

6315
07:45:19.360 --> 07:45:22.520
cars so their relatives can visit or they
can get to work.

6316
07:45:22.760 --> 07:45:27.720
At the moment we are just creating extra
aggression on the roads,

6317
07:45:27.960 --> 07:45:33.940
the last thing we need in terms of people
responding because if

6318
07:45:33.940 --> 07:45:37.380
someone does something untoward on the
road and

6319
07:45:37.540 --> 07:45:42.760
already agitated, you will get madder and
respond in a way that you would not

6320
07:45:42.760 --> 07:45:43.420
normally do.

6321
07:45:45.120 --> 07:45:51.020
We also need more work on graduated
penalties for repeat non-compliant

6322
07:45:51.020 --> 07:45:51.660
offenders

6323
07:45:52.940 --> 07:45:57.980
and issues like managing unregulated
e-scooters and e-bikes.

6324
07:45:57.980 --> 07:46:03.300
Again, that is about catching them rather
than some welcome legislation that we have

6325
07:46:03.300 --> 07:46:05.000
coming later this year in that regard.

6326
07:46:05.600 --> 07:46:07.510
Others have mentioned the quality of the
roads.

6327
07:46:07.510 --> 07:46:08.560
I second that.

6328
07:46:08.700 --> 07:46:10.920
Some of the roads are in very bad nick.

6329
07:46:11.280 --> 07:46:17.220
Again, I have a personal bugbear about
what seem to be very low speed limits

6330
07:46:17.220 --> 07:46:18.960
on dual carriageways.

6331
07:46:19.260 --> 07:46:21.980
I know traffic has to be managed,
including heavy traffic like

6332
07:46:21.980 --> 07:46:26.520
the M50, for example, where you cannot go
too fast or you will crash, especially in

6333
07:46:26.520 --> 07:46:30.960
the rain, but sometimes the speed limit on
good-quality roads seems to be quite low

6334
07:46:30.980 --> 07:46:31.260
and then

6335
07:46:31.260 --> 07:46:34.200
the regional roads it is way too high.

6336
07:46:34.200 --> 07:46:38.280
Some work, I have to acknowledge, has been
done on that, but we need more.

6337
07:46:38.680 --> 07:46:41.680
We need more in terms of training in
pursuit.

6338
07:46:41.680 --> 07:46:45.640
Deputy Tóibín mentioned the six gardaí who
will be trained by the end of this year.

6339
07:46:45.640 --> 07:46:51.340
That is too little too late in terms of
trying to catch people out and about

6340
07:46:51.340 --> 07:46:56.780
doing robberies and going up the wrong way
on dual carriageways, as we have

6341
07:46:56.780 --> 07:46:58.000
tragically seen recently.

6342
07:46:59.540 --> 07:47:04.780
On the insurance issue, I notice that the
Motor Insurers Bureau

6343
07:47:04.780 --> 07:47:10.740
of Ireland has information that can be
shared with the Garda in terms

6344
07:47:10.740 --> 07:47:14.840
