but I would love to see insurance discs

6345
07:47:14.840 --> 07:47:18.480
gone as well as the motor tax discs on
cars.

6346
07:47:19.120 --> 07:47:23.060
There should be a way of working that,
maybe not in this legislation but soon.

6347
07:47:24.360 --> 07:47:27.780
Broadly, I welcome the Bill but we have to
put resourcing into enforcement as well.

6348
07:47:27.900 --> 07:47:30.240
thank the

6349
07:47:30.240 --> 07:47:37.020
Minister

6350
07:47:37.020 --> 07:47:39.980
for being here and introducing this Bill.

6351
07:47:40.560 --> 07:47:46.400
I will start by acknowledging the 134
deaths this year and the families

6352
07:47:46.400 --> 07:47:49.260
who have lost their loved ones.

6353
07:47:49.900 --> 07:47:51.320
I welcome the Bill.

6354
07:47:51.320 --> 07:47:54.980
There are a number of practical changes in
it that I support.

6355
07:47:54.980 --> 07:48:00.280
It removes the outdated requirement to
display a paper motor tax disc, reflecting

6356
07:48:00.280 --> 07:48:04.920
the fact that gardaí can now check tax
status electronically through automatic

6357
07:48:04.920 --> 07:48:06.020
numberplate recognition.

6358
07:48:06.320 --> 07:48:07.620
That is a great positive.

6359
07:48:08.080 --> 07:48:12.880
It strengthens Check My Vehicle, giving
people buying a second-hand car better

6360
07:48:12.880 --> 07:48:17.260
access to official information on a
vehicle's tax and roadworthiness status.

6361
07:48:17.760 --> 07:48:21.860
It allows local authorities to access
collision data so they can identify

6362
07:48:21.860 --> 07:48:25.400
dangerous locations and better target road
safety improvements.

6363
07:48:26.260 --> 07:48:29.420
This is critical to all our communities.

6364
07:48:30.000 --> 07:48:35.220
I think we have all been in positions
where we have flagged areas that are

6365
07:48:35.220 --> 07:48:38.800
potential black spots for accidents.

6366
07:48:40.200 --> 07:48:46.160
Anything we can do to join up all the
agencies involved in road safety

6367
07:48:48.260 --> 07:48:48.900
is a positive.

6368
07:48:50.180 --> 07:48:56.000
also allows mobile camera van operators to
provide certificate evidence rather than

6369
07:48:56.000 --> 07:48:56.980
routinely attending court.

6370
07:48:56.980 --> 07:49:02.940
I will speak about court efficiency later
but, obviously, that is

6371
07:49:02.940 --> 07:49:04.970
very much an improvement.

6372
07:49:05.400 --> 07:49:10.520
Importantly, it allows a jury to return a
verdict of careless driving where somebody

6373
07:49:10.520 --> 07:49:14.720
has been charged with dangerous driving
but the evidence supports the lesser

6374
07:49:14.720 --> 07:49:15.180
offence.

6375
07:49:15.180 --> 07:49:17.267
This reform arises from Mr.

6376
07:49:17.267 --> 07:49:19.670
Justice Haughton's report into the tragic
death of Shane

6377
07:49:21.060 --> 07:49:26.040
There is a significant gap in our road
traffic enforcement system that I want to

6378
07:49:26.040 --> 07:49:26.520
focus on today.

6379
07:49:26.720 --> 07:49:28.360
It will not be a surprise to

6380
07:49:28.580 --> 07:49:34.540
I thank him for his Department's
engagement with me on this issue.

6381
07:49:34.740 --> 07:49:38.680
It relates to court penalty points, which
I have raised with

6382
07:49:38.680 --> 07:49:39.140
before.

6383
07:49:39.820 --> 07:49:44.040
When a court imposes penalty points, we
should be able to say with certainty that

6384
07:49:44.040 --> 07:49:49.460
the sanction actually reaches that
driver's record, and at present we

6385
07:49:49.460 --> 07:49:52.400
cannot.

6386
07:49:52.400 --> 07:49:55.680
Today's debate is about the national
vehicle and driver file.

6387
07:49:56.440 --> 07:50:01.200
I know Deputies are coming to this debate
with road safety

6388
07:50:01.200 --> 07:50:02.800
in general

6389
07:50:02.900 --> 07:50:05.600
but I am trying to focus on the NVDF.

6390
07:50:05.600 --> 07:50:10.000
As the Minister of State knows, I have
been pushing the issue of recording court

6391
07:50:10.000 --> 07:50:15.860
penalty points since I started to engage
with Susan Gray of PARC Road Safety Group.

6392
07:50:16.280 --> 07:50:22.100
The figures for 2024 that the Department

6393
07:50:22.100 --> 07:50:26.740
worked on show that almost half of
court-issued penalty points were not fully

6394
07:50:26.740 --> 07:50:30.440
captured on the national vehicle and
driver file.

6395
07:50:30.440 --> 07:50:33.060
It is important to put those figures in
context.

6396
07:50:33.060 --> 07:50:37.610
They include Irish licence holders,
foreign licence holders and people who do

6397
07:50:37.610 --> 07:50:40.440
not hold a driving licence at all.

6398
07:50:41.440 --> 07:50:42.960
We know that

6399
07:50:44.640 --> 07:50:50.460
a certain number of court penalty points
are not going to get to the

6400
07:50:50.460 --> 07:50:51.500
NVDF.

6401
07:50:51.500 --> 07:50:56.710
At the same time, the Department's own
analysis found that 19%

6402
07:50:57.360 --> 07:51:03.160
of unmatched court penalty point offences
in 2024 and 2025 could have been matched

6403
07:51:03.160 --> 07:51:08.540
to an existing driver record and that
potentially represents about

6404
07:51:08.540 --> 07:51:11.520
1,500 penalty points per year.

6405
07:51:12.440 --> 07:51:17.860
This is particularly serious because the
NVDF is the database that

6406
07:51:17.880 --> 07:51:21.860
and motor insurers rely on to establish a

6407
07:51:21.860 --> 07:51:22.420
status.

6408
07:51:23.080 --> 07:51:27.520
The system works much better when an
offence is dealt with through fixed charge

6409
07:51:27.520 --> 07:51:31.080
notices because the driver number is
captured from the start.

6410
07:51:31.500 --> 07:51:34.770
The serious weakness arises when the cases
go through the courts.

6411
07:51:40.280 --> 07:51:43.020
and their driver number may not be
collected.

